 "co_the_crestones_the_prow_kit_carson": {
  "area": "co_the_crestones",
  "set": {
   "approach": "The usual way in is the Spanish Creek trail, which starts at the Crestone Mountain Zen Center's upper parking lot on private land, so the landowner's rules apply and a wilderness access permit is needed. The trail follows Spanish Creek and crosses it several times, with a blowdown section and cairns. Camp near treeline below the lower buttress of the Prow. The Prow is a fin on the southwest ridge of Kit Carson. Stay on the east side of it while approaching to avoid getting cliffed out.",
   "descent_text": "From the top, where a large ledge gives access to Kit Carson and Challenger Point, walk east over another peak to the broad low valley between Kit Carson and Ellingwood, which leads back toward camp. Do not turn down too early, because that line meets steep slabs."
  },
